From unknown 11 Aug 1997 23:41:26 -0000
Message-ID: <lbsowgs2li.fsf@surf.usc.edu>
Date: 11 Aug 1997 23:41:26 -0000
From: Terrence Brannon
Subject: Quick Note for the Novices

If you manage to get RedHat's Installation Menu up via the
MILO-vmlinux.gz-ramdisk sequence, then you can hit alt-F2 after a few
screens to get a root unix prompt. Your removeable media will be
mounted in tmp as fd0 and (in my case --- JAZ drive) sdb1

You can then do fdisk, mke2fs, and copy things between them --- as I
must do since no one split the base distribution into floppy sizes.

